{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Live DC rich-text lane: outbound echo re-diffs against stale JQL search snapshot\n\n## Observed failure\n`tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_rich_text_live.py::test_live_rich_text_renders_and_echo_is_safe`\nand `::test_live_rich_text_both_sides_conflict_keeps_local` fail on the dispatched Live External\nIntegration run (33052311279, DC lane), both with:\n`AssertionError: the index never reflected the pushed body ... within 240s (120 attempts)`.\nThe indexed doc shows `description: None` and `updated` stuck at the binding step.\n\n## Corrected root cause (supersedes the \"index lag / widen the wait\" framing of bug 2c60)\nThe test's `_push_and_converge` blocks on `_wait_until_search_reflects` — waiting for the JQL\nSEARCH index to reflect the pushed `description`. That guards a REAL dependency: the outbound\nFIELD differ (`compute_outbound_mutations`, outbound_differ.py) diffs local tickets against the\nFETCHER'S JQL-SEARCH SNAPSHOT (`fetcher.fetch_snapshot` -> `search_issues`). For a key PRESENT in\nthe snapshot (ours is — its key is indexed for existence via `wait_until_searchable`), the differ\ncompares local `description` against the SNAPSHOT's `description`, which is STALE (`None`) until\nthe background Lucene reindex catches up. Direct GET (`_safe_get_issue` / `get_issue_by_rest`,\nimmediately consistent) is used ONLY for bound-but-ABSENT keys, not bound-and-present ones. So on\nthe ephemeral DC — whose background reindex is UNBOUNDED (ADR 0037 s3) and, on a starved instance,\nnever reflects the write within any fixed budget — the echo pass re-diffs the just-pushed field as\nchanged and would churn, and the wait times out.\n\nTwo prior fixes (2c60: widen to 240s; then force a per-issue reindex) both targeted search\nVISIBILITY. Widening cannot bound an unbounded wait, and the forced-reindex helper had NO effect\n(and no observability — it no-ops silently), likely because `/rest/api/2/reindex/issue` is not an\neffective synchronous foreground reindex on DC 8.17. The fix must remove the dependence on\nunbounded search visibility, not chase it.\n\n## Candidate resolutions (to be decided by investigation + history)\n1. PRODUCT: outbound differ confirms a snapshot-detected field change via a bounded direct GET\n   before emitting the mutation, so a stale-snapshot false-positive cannot cause churn (extends\n   the existing bound-but-absent direct-GET seam to bound-and-present keys). Robust for ANY\n   eventually-consistent remote.\n2. HARNESS: configure the ephemeral Jira DC for synchronous/fast indexing at boot.\n3. TEST: verify the landed body via a direct GET (immediately consistent) and re-express echo-\n   safety so it does not depend on unbounded search visibility.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [x] Root cause confirmed (which of 1/2/3, with history/ADR support).\n- [x] Fix removes the unbounded-search-visibility dependency; a held-out test proves it with teeth.\n- [x] [non-codebase] A dispatched Live External Integration run shows the DC lane GREEN (both\n      rich-text tests pass) AND the Cloud mutation lane GREEN. Run URL commented here.\n      provenance: environment=github-actions external-integration.yml run 33137402410 on main at 6fe5c0d54574 (contains the fix 3b92fad7); principal=github-actions workflow_dispatch runner against the ephemeral Jira DC harness and the real Jira Cloud coordinator project; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — Job 98740362395 (jira DC harness smoke) concluded success with PASSED test_live_rich_text_renders_and_echo_is_safe and PASSED test_live_rich_text_both_sides_conflict_keeps_local (74 passed, neither skipped); the jira Cloud coordinator mutation probe job also concluded success.\n- [x] `make lint && make typecheck && make test` green."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787964071478682001,"uuid":"eb36babf-4600-4b97-87f2-e1d823389661"}